  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of a right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $\u2220B,$ we have the length of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}$ and need to determine the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061({70}^{\u2218}) & =\\frac{6}{BC} \\\\ BC\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}\u2061({70}^{\u2218}) & =6 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({70}^{\u2218})} \\\\ BC & =2.183\u2026\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot (2.183\u2026) \\\\  & =6.551\u2026 \\\\  & \u22487,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.",
